                    G A B C I ' S   A C O U S T I C   C L O A K
        ---------------------------------------------------------------
                 Phase-Rotation Sidechain Engine · VST3 / Standalone

  DESCRIPTION
  -----------
  Acoustic Cloak replaces traditional sidechain ducking with a real-time
  phase-rotation engine: instead of lowering the bass's volume on every
  kick hit, it measures the actual phase relationship between kick and
  bass inside an adjustable low-frequency window and rotates the bass's
  phase so the two signals sum CONSTRUCTIVELY. Result: full loudness,
  zero gain reduction, no pumping. A flat-summing Linkwitz-Riley crossover
  isolates the target band; an allpass Hilbert transformer provides an
  exact analytic (I/Q) signal for the rotation; a "Dummy All-Pass" trick
  warps the untouched residual by an identical filter copy, so the
  recombination stays magnitude-flat at ANY rotation angle. A live
  polar "Holographic Radar" shows the measured phase/correlation.

  MAIN PARAMETERS
  ----------------
  Cloak Depth ........... 0-100%   strength of the applied phase correction
  Lookahead ............. 0-20ms   pre-delay budget for analysis/correction
  Target Freq Low/High .. 20-300Hz the frequency window the engine works in
  Transient Sensitivity .. 0-100%  how readily kick transients gate the
                                    correction's adaptation speed
  Bypass ................. on/off  click-free (20ms crossfade) true dry
                                    passthrough

  KEY TECHNOLOGY
  ---------------
  * BandIsolator          - 2-stage 4th-order Linkwitz-Riley crossover,
                             flat-sum verified within +/-2% (10Hz-8kHz)
  * AllpassHilbertNetwork - 8-stage interleaved IIR allpass Hilbert
                             transformer, EXACT magnitude preservation
                             (|H(f)|=1 always), no resonant image leakage
  * "Dummy All-Pass"      - identical-cascade residual warp; LTI linearity
                             (filter(A)+filter(B)=filter(A+B)) guarantees
                             a flat recombination at any rotation angle
  * PhaseCorrelationAnalyzer - continuous phase-difference tracking with
                             a broadband, non-resonant transient gate
  * Holographic Radar GUI - live polar phase/correlation display,
                             phosphor-glow "medical instrument" aesthetic

  QUALITY (measured, not assumed)
  ---------------------------------
  Automated test assertions .......... 78, across 14 test cases, all pass
  BandIsolator flat-sum accuracy ...... within 2% (10Hz-8kHz sweep)
  AllpassHilbertNetwork phase accuracy  80-84 deg of 90 (20-150Hz band)
  AllpassHilbertNetwork magnitude error  exact (allpass: |H(f)|=1 always)
  Estimated single-instance CPU ....... 0.522% @ 48kHz/512 samples
  Design history .................... 3 independent review cycles; two
                                        earlier architectures (resonator
                                        -bank reconstruction, nested
                                        crossover sub-bands) were built,
                                        measured, and discarded on hard
                                        evidence -- see CHANGELOG.md

